d":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1819,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["bazel","build","build-system","correct","fast","multi-language","scalable","test"],"visibility":"public","forks":4359,"open_issues":1819,"watchers":24886,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Bazel repeatedly hangs when fetching large external git repositories (defined in the WORKSPACE file with git_repository). At some point the object count reported in the console (as in INFO: Cloning https://github.com/grpc/grpc.git: Receiving objects (171939 / 255634)) gets stuck and does not increase for 10+ minutes, or even for hours. This problem occurs non-deterministically, however when it does, it typically does at the same object count (eg. 171939).\r\n\r\nI think this occurs more often when the network is slow or when the git hosting service (github) is under heavy load (?). Also, the cause might be in git: Cloning the same repository directly with git command-line client (git clone https://github.com/grpc/grpc.git) also hangs randomly.\r\n\r\nPossibly related issues:\r\nhttps://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/1760\r\nhttps://groups.google.com/forum/#!msg/bazel-discuss/5LOE_kYkoyo/rkOLjMVaCAAJ. \r\n\r\nAs a workaround, would it be possible to have Bazel support shallow git clones, without the history of older commits? See git clone --depth=0 and git archive.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/2696/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/2696/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]